   $q$A box of 10 light bulbs contains 3 defective bulbs. An inspector picks 2 bulbs at random without replacement. Let $X$ be the number of defective bulbs picked. What is $E(X)$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$1$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"averaged-values-ignoring-probabilities"},{"text":"$0.3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-one-draw"},{"text":"$\\frac{21}{45}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-probability-of-one-defective"},{"text":"$0.6$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$0.6$$q$, $q$$P(X = 1) = \frac{3 \cdot 7}{45} = \frac{21}{45}$ and $P(X = 2) = \frac{3}{45}$, so $E(X) = \frac{21}{45} + 2 \cdot \frac{3}{45} = \frac{27}{45} = 0.6$. The choice $0.3$ is the expected count for one draw, not two.$q$, 'draft', null)
